<title>PAKISTAN: Pakistan's new cotton crop starts arriving.</title>
<headline>Pakistan's new cotton crop starts arriving.</headline>
<dateline>KARACHI, Pakistan 1997-06-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>The first cotton from Pakistan's new crop arrived at a ginning factory overnight and dealers said domestic prices could fall as a result.</p>
<p>Nasim Usman, a dealer at the private Karachi Cotton Association, said the crop, which had been due to arrive in early July, had ripened early due to hot weather in the southern province of Sindh. The first lot of 100 375-lb bales of NIAB-78 reached a ginning factory in Chichavatni in Punjab province.</p>
<p>Usman said some ginning units would start work in Sindh next week. Prices of old-crop cotton might dip 50 rupees ($1.23) per maund (37.32 kg) soon. -- Ibrahim Khan 9221-5685192</p>
</text>
